{"raw": {"https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d098156f9c01982e34a60801d2&id=8a78839e9f443598019f4dbb219619b9&source=&lang=en": {"title": "ASN Chairperson - Cresson", "description": "Careers | Mount Aloysius College Home Position: ASN Chairperson - Cresson Location: Cresson, PA Job Id: 227 # of Openings: 1 Mount Aloysius College, repeatedly recognized by ModernThink as a \"Great College to Work For,\u201d invites applications from highly qualified individuals to join our leadership team in the School of Nursing as the ASN Chairperson beginning August 2026/Fall 2026 in Cresson, PA. Current Opening Reporting to the Dean of Nursing, the ASN Chairperson provides departmental oversight and clinical coordination of the College\u2019s Associate of Science in Nursing program, based in Cresson, PA.\u00a0 This position is responsible to ensure that the ASN program\u2019s curriculum and outcomes align with the guidelines of Accreditation Commission for Education in Nursing (ACEN) and the PA State Board of Nursing.\u00a0 This includes modeling good instruction, including integration of technology, development of quality course syllabi, establishing policy and procedures within the program, and assisting others within the ASN program with these matters. This position also holds teaching responsibilities within the ASN program. This position requires a regular, full-time 10-month appointment from August \u2013 May, with additional required workdays during the summer at the beginning and end of the core academic year.\u00a0 The ASN Chairperson is responsible for a workload of 24 credits or equivalent, which includes a 21-credit release for administrative duties, per academic year, and supervises all full-time and part-time faculty assigned to the ASN Program. Faculty are expected to have a regular presence on campus (5 days per week required) to engage with students both inside and outside of the classroom. In addition to teaching, the ASN Chairperson is responsible to lead departmental initiatives, recruit and mentor adjunct faculty, and assure courses are properly resourced with appropriate academic quality and rigor.\u00a0 Also participates in department meetings, committee work, advises students academically, holds regular office hours, and assists with College events, service to the College, and other activities. Mount Aloysius College offers a generous benefits package for full-time employees including but not limited to: medical/health, dental, vision, and life insurance; short-term and long-term disability insurance; Retirement plan match; tuition remission; and an employee assistance program, among others. Qualifications Master's degree in Nursing (MSN) required.\u00a0 Doctorate preferred (PhD, DNP, EdD) earned or in final semester/ABD with pending graduation date.\u00a0 Two (2) to three (3) years of leadership experience in nursing education administration required.\u00a0 Prior classroom and clinical teaching experience at the collegiate level required. Valid, unencumbered license as a registered nurse or advanced practice nurse in Pennsylvania required. Minimum 3-4 years of nursing experience and a demonstrated ability to perform at a high level is required. A strong student focus is required, with the ability to relay information effectively.\u00a0 Excellent oral and written communication skills are expected.\u00a0 Proficiency with Microsoft Word and Excel is required. Must be able to work with minimal supervision and demonstrate the ability to prioritize, multitask, maintain attention to detail orientation, and excel in a fast-paced, high volume office.\u00a0 High degree of professionalism and a demonstrated ability to maintain high ethical standards and confidentiality is required. Proficiency in curriculum design, evaluation, instruction, program administration, and academic advising also preferred.\u00a0 Faculty rank is dependent upon education, experience and credentials. This role is not budgeted for visa sponsorship at this time; all candidates must be authorized to work in the US at the time of submission of their application. About Mount Aloysius College Mount Aloysius College ( www.mtaloy.edu ) is a private, comprehensive Catholic college located in Pennsylvania\u2019s Laurel Highlands, serving a diverse community of learners. The College has a long history of responding to community needs through relevant academic programs and community service. Mount Aloysius is located on a 193-acre campus in Cresson, PA, Cambria County. Founded in 1853 by the Dublin, Ireland-based Religious Sisters of Mercy, Mount Aloysius is one of 17 such institutions in the United States and is a member of the Conference for Mercy Higher Education (CMHE). The College provides small class sizes, and students benefit from a highly engaged faculty and staff. The School of Nursing and Health Sciences offers a real-world experience for nursing students on site at Mount Aloysius College.\u00a0 Our facilities include a four-room simulation nursing unit, interactive manikins and realistic hospital systems (including a state-of-the-art anatomage table).\u00a0 Built-in observation units, modern study and lounge areas create inviting study spaces for students and support a personalized learning experience for each student.\u00a0 Additionally, we are thrilled to offer an unprecedented opportunity for future nurses through the Future Heroes Nursing Scholarship, in partnership with UPMC Altoona, Bedford & Somerset.\u00a0 To learn more about our nursing program and the Future Heroes Nursing Scholarship, please follow the links below: Nursing Program Overview - Mount Aloysius College Future Heroes Nursing Scholarship Initiative in affiliation with UPMC - Mount Aloysius College Commitment to Diversity Mount Aloysius is committed to building an inclusive community that values each person and respects diversity of all kinds \u2013 diversity of thought, experience, culture, ethnicity, religion, gender/gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, etc. to create a workplace where everyone participates and is able to contribute their own unique gifts, talents and perspectives. Application Instructions Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled.\u00a0 All applicants should submit a resume with accompanying cover letter via the Mount Aloysius College website at http://www.mtaloy.edu/employment-opportunities/. Applicants needing reasonable accommodation to participate in the application process should contact the Office of Human Resources at (814) 886-6519. Mount Aloysius College is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by REQUIRED NOTICES The Mount Aloysius College Annual Security and Fire Safety Report contains statistics for the three previous calendar years of reported crimes that occurred on our campuses, in certain off-campus buildings or properties owned or controlled by Mount Aloysius College, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from our campuses. This annual report is required by federal law, and contains information regarding campus security and personal safety, including institutional policies, crime prevention, crime reporting policies, and fire safety. The report also includes our current Sexual Assault and Misconduct Policies. The 2024 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online. You may also request a printed copy from Mount Aloysius College's Office of Campus Safety, located in Ihmsen Hall 112, by calling (814) 886-6327 or via email to CampusSafety@mtaloy.edu EEO is the LAW Mount Aloysius College is an equal opportunity employer, and does not tolerate unlawful discrimination against any person on the basis of age, ancestry, color, disability or handicap, national origin, race, religious creed, gender, sexual orientation, genetic information or veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact us at 814-886-6500 or by email at HumanResources@mtaloy.edu. Employment will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with College policy. Mount Aloysius College"}, "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d098156f9c01982e34a60801d2&id=8a78839ea06420ea01a068ae6d3432f9&source=&lang=en": {"title": "Adjunct Faculty - Medical Terminology", "description": "Careers | Mount Aloysius College Home Position: Adjunct Faculty - Medical Terminology Location: Cresson, PA Job Id: 231 # of Openings: 1 Adjunct Faculty \u2013 Medical Terminology (Cresson) Current Opening Mount Aloysius College, repeatedly recognized by ModernThink as a \u201cGreat College to Work For,\u201d is searching for qualified candidates to teach undergraduate Medical Terminology coursework on an adjunct basis during the 2026-2027 Academic Year.\u00a0 Opportunities exist in multiple content areas. Each 15-week course is scheduled to be taught in person at our Cresson location during daytime hours.\u00a0 Sections will be offered twice a week, Monday/Wednesday or Tuesday/Thursday, depending on need. Faculty are expected to create an interactive, student-centered learning environment in the classroom.\u00a0 Some basic course materials should be made available to students using the Canvas Learning Management System. Adjunct faculty at Mount Aloysius College may participate in our retirement savings plan, and are eligible for limited tuition remission benefits for themselves and their dependents.\u00a0 As an Adjunct faculty member, you also receive complimentary access to our wellness center/gym, are eligible for the Employee Assistance Program (EAP) and have access to various employee discounts. Qualifications Master\u2019s degree or graduate degree in a related field such as Nursing, Public Health, Health Sciences, Physician Assistant Studies, Physical Therapy, Occupational Therapy or other related field, and at least two (2) years of relevant classroom teaching experience is required.\u00a0 Collegiate teaching experience is highly preferred.\u00a0 An equivalent combination of applicable teaching experience and education will be considered.\u00a0 Experience using Canvas Learning Management System, or similar LMS preferred.\u00a0 Must have the ability to remain flexible, employ a range of teaching methods, and effectively incorporate technology into the teaching/learning process.\u00a0 Strong interpersonal and both oral and written communication skills, organizational and record-keeping skills necessary. Adjunct appointments are\u00a0single-semester opportunities only, with no guarantee of future appointments. This role is not budgeted for visa sponsorship at this time; all candidates must be authorized to work in the US at the time of submission of their application. About Mount Aloysius College Mount Aloysius College (www.mtaloy.edu) is a private, comprehensive Catholic college located in Pennsylvania\u2019s Laurel Highlands, serving a diverse community of learners. The College has a long history of responding to community needs through relevant academic programs and community service. Mount Aloysius is located on a 193-acre campus in Cresson, PA, Cambria County. Founded in 1853 by the Dublin, Ireland-based Religious Sisters of Mercy, Mount Aloysius is one of 17 such institutions in the United States and is a member of the Conference for Mercy Higher Education (CMHE). The College provides small class sizes, and students benefit from a highly engaged faculty and staff. Commitment to Diversity Mount Aloysius is committed to building an inclusive community that values each person and respects diversity of all kinds \u2013 diversity of thought, experience, culture, ethnicity, religion, gender/gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, etc. to create a workplace where everyone participates and is able to contribute their own unique gifts, talents and perspectives. Application Instructions Qualified candidates should submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, and three professional references in confidence to the Office of Human Resources via their online application.\u00a0 Review of applications will begin immediately and applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Applicants needing reasonable accommodation to participate in the application process should contact the Office of Human Resources at 814-886-6494. Mount Aloysius College is an Equal Opportunity Employer Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by REQUIRED NOTICES The Mount Aloysius College Annual Security and Fire Safety Report contains statistics for the three previous calendar years of reported crimes that occurred on our campuses, in certain off-campus buildings or properties owned or controlled by Mount Aloysius College, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from our campuses. This annual report is required by federal law, and contains information regarding campus security and personal safety, including institutional policies, crime prevention, crime reporting policies, and fire safety. The report also includes our current Sexual Assault and Misconduct Policies. The 2024 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online. You may also request a printed copy from Mount Aloysius College's Office of Campus Safety, located in Ihmsen Hall 112, by calling (814) 886-6327 or via email to CampusSafety@mtaloy.edu EEO is the LAW Mount Aloysius College is an equal opportunity employer, and does not tolerate unlawful discrimination against any person on the basis of age, ancestry, color, disability or handicap, national origin, race, religious creed, gender, sexual orientation, genetic information or veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact us at 814-886-6500 or by email at HumanResources@mtaloy.edu. Employment will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with College policy. Mount Aloysius College"}, "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d098156f9c01982e34a60801d2&id=8a78839ea06420ea01a090d15b3f22df&source=&lang=en": {"title": "Administrative Coordinator - DuBois", "description": "Careers | Mount Aloysius College Home Position: Administrative Coordinator - DuBois Location: DuBois, PA Job Id: 233 # of Openings: 1 Mount Aloysius College, repeatedly recognized by ModernThink as a \u201cGreat College to Work For,\u201d seeks a highly skilled and organized individual to serve as the Administrative Coordinator for Nursing, Surgical Technology, and Medical Imaging programs, beginning August 2026/Fall 2026 in DuBois, PA. Current Opening The Administrative Coordinator is responsible for a variety of high-level clerical and administrative duties to support the Nursing, Surg-Tech, and Medical Imaging teams in DuBois and to ensure consistent and efficient operations in all DuBois programs. This role requires significant coordination responsibilities and the ability to accurately track and organize a variety of data for compliance and reporting purposes using Excel and/or Google Sheets.\u00a0 Also prepares signature-ready letters, revises handbooks and other procedural documents as assigned. The Administrative Coordinator communicates and corresponds regularly with clinical sites and agency partners.\u00a0 Also assists with planning and coordination of special events and programs.\u00a0 Maintains confidential files across all DuBois programs, including management of demographic information and ensures that all required student and faculty documentation/licensure is current and accurately filed. This position also assists with departmental website updates, gathers and organizes documentation for the academic appeals process, directs callers and visitors as appropriate, schedules meetings, and disseminates mail.\u00a0 Also responsible to enter budget requests, submit purchase requisitions, and place supply orders. May interview prospective work-study students, and provide supervision to assigned students. This is a full-time, year-round, benefit-eligible position. While some flexibility in scheduling exists, this position is on campus in DuBois, PA (5 days per week required), and is not eligible for remote work. Qualifications Bachelor\u2019s degree and two (2) years of experience in executive or high-level administrative support roles required. Previous experience working in a secondary or post-secondary education setting is preferred. Equivalent combination of education and experience will be considered. Above average verbal, written, interpersonal and organizational skills required; Proficiency in Google Suite, Microsoft Office Suite, and AdobeSign required. Advanced skills in Microsoft Word and Excel desired.\u00a0 Demonstrated ability to prioritize, multitask, maintain attention to detail orientation, and excel in a fast-paced, high volume office with little to no supervision is required.\u00a0 The successful candidate must be able to work collaboratively with others and exercise independent thinking.\u00a0 Should be able to foresee risks and anticipate needs, and make sound decisions.\u00a0 Ability to quickly and efficiently learn software that is highly utilized within the Higher Education space required.\u00a0 High degree of professionalism and a demonstrated ability to maintain high ethical standards and confidentiality is required. This role is not budgeted for visa sponsorship at this time; all candidates must be authorized to\u00a0work in the US at the time of submission of their application. About Mount Aloysius College\u2019s Expansion into DuBois, PA Mount Aloysius College is bringing nursing education to DuBois beginning Fall 2026!\u00a0 Students can complete pre-nursing coursework this fall, and begin their path toward a rewarding healthcare career close to home with a two year associates degree. Through a new collaboration with Penn Highlands Healthcare, eligible nursing students may receive up to $48,000 in combined financial support, along with hands-on clinical opportunities and pathways to employment after graduation. Students can also apply for our radiography and surgical technology programs in DuBois, both of which are also in partnership with Penn Highlands Healthcare. Commitment to Diversity Mount Aloysius is committed to building an inclusive community that values each person and respects diversity of all kinds \u2013 diversity of thought, experience, culture, ethnicity, religion, gender/gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, etc. to create a workplace where everyone participates and is able to contribute their own unique gifts, talents and perspectives. Application Instructions Apply online at http://www.mtaloy.edu/employment-opportunities.\u00a0 All applicants should submit a resume with an accompanying cover letter.\u00a0 Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled.\u00a0 Applicants needing reasonable accommodation to participate in the application process should contact the Office of Human Resources at (814) 886-6519. Mount Aloysius College is an Equal Opportunity Employer Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by REQUIRED NOTICES The Mount Aloysius College Annual Security and Fire Safety Report contains statistics for the three previous calendar years of reported crimes that occurred on our campuses, in certain off-campus buildings or properties owned or controlled by Mount Aloysius College, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from our campuses. This annual report is required by federal law, and contains information regarding campus security and personal safety, including institutional policies, crime prevention, crime reporting policies, and fire safety. The report also includes our current Sexual Assault and Misconduct Policies. The 2024 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online. You may also request a printed copy from Mount Aloysius College's Office of Campus Safety, located in Ihmsen Hall 112, by calling (814) 886-6327 or via email to CampusSafety@mtaloy.edu EEO is the LAW Mount Aloysius College is an equal opportunity employer, and does not tolerate unlawful discrimination against any person on the basis of age, ancestry, color, disability or handicap, national origin, race, religious creed, gender, sexual orientation, genetic information or veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact us at 814-886-6500 or by email at HumanResources@mtaloy.edu. Employment will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with College policy. Mount Aloysius College"}, "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d098156f9c01982e34a60801d2&id=8a78839fa064212401a0ab4750b47ef2&source=&lang=en": {"title": "Adjunct Instructor - Math 111 The Three C's - Cresson", "description": "Careers | Mount Aloysius College Home Position: Adjunct Instructor - Math 111 The Three C's - Cresson Location: Cresson, PA Job Id: 238 # of Openings: 1 Current Opening Mount Aloysius College, repeatedly recognized by ModernThink as a \u201cGreat College to Work For,\u201d is searching for qualified candidates to teach undergraduate Math 111 - The Three C\u2019s coursework on an adjunct basis during the 2026-2027 Academic Year. Each 15-week course is scheduled to be taught in person at our Cresson location during daytime hours.\u00a0 Sections may be offered twice a week or three times a week, depending on need. Online teaching opportunities may be available for such courses in the future. Faculty are expected to create an interactive, student-centered learning environment in the classroom.\u00a0 Some basic course materials should be made available to students using the Canvas Learning Management System. Adjunct faculty at Mount Aloysius College may participate in our retirement savings plan, and are eligible for limited tuition remission benefits for themselves and their dependents.\u00a0 As an Adjunct faculty member, you also receive complimentary access to our wellness center/gym, are eligible for the Employee Assistance Program (EAP) and have access to various employee discounts. Qualifications Master\u2019s degree in Mathematics or related field and at least two (2) years of relevant classroom teaching experience is preferred.\u00a0 Collegiate teaching experience is highly preferred.\u00a0 An equivalent combination of applicable teaching experience and education will be considered.\u00a0 Experience using Canvas Learning Management System, or similar LMS preferred.\u00a0 Must have the ability to remain flexible, employ a range of teaching methods, and effectively incorporate technology into the teaching/learning process.\u00a0 Strong interpersonal and both oral and written communication skills, organizational and record-keeping skills necessary. Adjunct appointments are\u00a0single-semester opportunities only, with no guarantee of future appointments. This role is not budgeted for visa sponsorship at this time; all candidates must be authorized to work in the US at the time of submission of their application. About Mount Aloysius College Mount Aloysius College (www.mtaloy.edu) is a private, comprehensive Catholic college located in Pennsylvania\u2019s Laurel Highlands, serving a diverse community of learners. The College has a long history of responding to community needs through relevant academic programs and community service. Mount Aloysius is located on a 193-acre campus in Cresson, PA, Cambria County. Founded in 1853 by the Dublin, Ireland-based Religious Sisters of Mercy, Mount Aloysius is one of 17 such institutions in the United States and is a member of the Conference for Mercy Higher Education (CMHE). The College provides small class sizes, and students benefit from a highly engaged faculty and staff. Commitment to Diversity Mount Aloysius is committed to building an inclusive community that values each person and respects diversity of all kinds \u2013 diversity of thought, experience, culture, ethnicity, religion, gender/gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, etc. to create a workplace where everyone participates and is able to contribute their own unique gifts, talents and perspectives. Application Instructions Qualified candidates should submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, and three professional references in confidence to the Office of Human Resources via their online application.\u00a0 Review of applications will begin immediately and applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Applicants needing reasonable accommodation to participate in the application process should contact the Office of Human Resources at 814-886-6494. Mount Aloysius College is an Equal Opportunity Employer Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by REQUIRED NOTICES The Mount Aloysius College Annual Security and Fire Safety Report contains statistics for the three previous calendar years of reported crimes that occurred on our campuses, in certain off-campus buildings or properties owned or controlled by Mount Aloysius College, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from our campuses. This annual report is required by federal law, and contains information regarding campus security and personal safety, including institutional policies, crime prevention, crime reporting policies, and fire safety. The report also includes our current Sexual Assault and Misconduct Policies. The 2024 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online. You may also request a printed copy from Mount Aloysius College's Office of Campus Safety, located in Ihmsen Hall 112, by calling (814) 886-6327 or via email to CampusSafety@mtaloy.edu EEO is the LAW Mount Aloysius College is an equal opportunity employer, and does not tolerate unlawful discrimination against any person on the basis of age, ancestry, color, disability or handicap, national origin, race, religious creed, gender, sexual orientation, genetic information or veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact us at 814-886-6500 or by email at HumanResources@mtaloy.edu. Employment will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with College policy. Mount Aloysius College"}, "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d098156f9c01982e34a60801d2&id=8a78839fa064212401a0ab4952727fce&source=&lang=en": {"title": "Adjunct Instructor - Math 111 The Three C's - DuBois", "description": "Careers | Mount Aloysius College Home Position: Adjunct Instructor - Math 111 The Three C's - DuBois Location: DuBois, PA Job Id: 239 # of Openings: 1 Current Opening Mount Aloysius College, repeatedly recognized by ModernThink as a \u201cGreat College to Work For,\u201d is searching for qualified candidates to teach undergraduate Math 111 - The Three C\u2019s coursework on an adjunct basis during the 2026-2027 Academic Year. Each 15-week course is scheduled to be taught in person at our DuBois location during daytime hours.\u00a0 Sections may be offered twice a week or three times a week, depending on need. Online teaching opportunities may be available for such courses in the future. Faculty are expected to create an interactive, student-centered learning environment in the classroom.\u00a0 Some basic course materials should be made available to students using the Canvas Learning Management System. Adjunct faculty at Mount Aloysius College may participate in our retirement savings plan, and are eligible for limited tuition remission benefits for themselves and their dependents.\u00a0 As an Adjunct faculty member, you also receive complimentary access to our wellness center/gym, are eligible for the Employee Assistance Program (EAP) and have access to various employee discounts. Qualifications Master\u2019s degree in Mathematics or related field and at least two (2) years of relevant classroom teaching experience is preferred.\u00a0 Collegiate teaching experience is highly preferred.\u00a0 An equivalent combination of applicable teaching experience and education will be considered.\u00a0 Experience using Canvas Learning Management System, or similar LMS preferred.\u00a0 Must have the ability to remain flexible, employ a range of teaching methods, and effectively incorporate technology into the teaching/learning process.\u00a0 Strong interpersonal and both oral and written communication skills, organizational and record-keeping skills necessary. Adjunct appointments are\u00a0single-semester opportunities only, with no guarantee of future appointments. This role is not budgeted for visa sponsorship at this time; all candidates must be authorized to work in the US at the time of submission of their application. About Mount Aloysius College Mount Aloysius College (www.mtaloy.edu) is a private, comprehensive Catholic college located in Pennsylvania\u2019s Laurel Highlands, serving a diverse community of learners. The College has a long history of responding to community needs through relevant academic programs and community service. Mount Aloysius is located on a 193-acre campus in Cresson, PA, Cambria County. Founded in 1853 by the Dublin, Ireland-based Religious Sisters of Mercy, Mount Aloysius is one of 17 such institutions in the United States and is a member of the Conference for Mercy Higher Education (CMHE). The College provides small class sizes, and students benefit from a highly engaged faculty and staff. Commitment to Diversity Mount Aloysius is committed to building an inclusive community that values each person and respects diversity of all kinds \u2013 diversity of thought, experience, culture, ethnicity, religion, gender/gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, etc. to create a workplace where everyone participates and is able to contribute their own unique gifts, talents and perspectives. Application Instructions Qualified candidates should submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, and three professional references in confidence to the Office of Human Resources via their online application.\u00a0 Review of applications will begin immediately and applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Applicants needing reasonable accommodation to participate in the application process should contact the Office of Human Resources at 814-886-6494. Mount Aloysius College is an Equal Opportunity Employer Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by REQUIRED NOTICES The Mount Aloysius College Annual Security and Fire Safety Report contains statistics for the three previous calendar years of reported crimes that occurred on our campuses, in certain off-campus buildings or properties owned or controlled by Mount Aloysius College, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from our campuses. This annual report is required by federal law, and contains information regarding campus security and personal safety, including institutional policies, crime prevention, crime reporting policies, and fire safety. The report also includes our current Sexual Assault and Misconduct Policies. The 2024 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online. You may also request a printed copy from Mount Aloysius College's Office of Campus Safety, located in Ihmsen Hall 112, by calling (814) 886-6327 or via email to CampusSafety@mtaloy.edu EEO is the LAW Mount Aloysius College is an equal opportunity employer, and does not tolerate unlawful discrimination against any person on the basis of age, ancestry, color, disability or handicap, national origin, race, religious creed, gender, sexual orientation, genetic information or veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact us at 814-886-6500 or by email at HumanResources@mtaloy.edu. Employment will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with College policy. Mount Aloysius College"}, "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d098156f9c01982e34a60801d2&id=8a78839fa0f425e701a0fe11f02a05bb&source=&lang=en": {"title": "ASN Chairperson - DuBois", "description": "Careers | Mount Aloysius College Home Position: ASN Chairperson - DuBois Location: DuBois, PA Job Id: 244 # of Openings: 1 Mount Aloysius College, repeatedly recognized by ModernThink as a \"Great College to Work For,\u201d invites applications from highly qualified individuals to join our leadership team in the School of Nursing as the ASN Chairperson beginning immediately in DuBois, PA. Current Opening Reporting to the Dean of Nursing, the ASN Chairperson provides departmental oversight and clinical coordination of the College\u2019s Associate of Science in Nursing program, based in DuBois, PA.\u00a0 This position is responsible to ensure that the ASN (DuBois) program\u2019s curriculum and outcomes align with the guidelines of Accreditation Commission for Education in Nursing (ACEN) and the PA State Board of Nursing.\u00a0 This includes modeling good instruction, including integration of technology, development of quality course syllabi, establishing policy and procedures within the program, and assisting others within the ASN program with these matters. This position also holds teaching responsibilities within the ASN program. This open faculty position offers a regular, full-time 10-month appointment from August \u2013 May, with additional required workdays during the summer at the beginning and end of the core academic year.\u00a0 The ASN Chairperson is responsible for a workload of 24 credits or equivalent, which includes a 9-credit release for administrative duties, per academic year, and supervises all full-time and part-time faculty assigned to the ASN Program in DuBois. Faculty are expected to have a regular presence on campus (5 days per week required) to engage with students both inside and outside of the classroom. In addition to teaching, the ASN Chairperson is responsible to lead departmental initiatives, recruit and mentor adjunct faculty, and assure courses are properly resourced with appropriate academic quality and rigor.\u00a0 Also participates in department meetings, committee work, advises students academically, holds regular office hours, and assists with College events, service to the College, and other activities. Mount Aloysius College offers a generous benefits package for full-time employees including but not limited to: medical/health, dental, vision, and life insurance; short-term and long-term disability insurance; Retirement plan match; tuition remission; and an employee assistance program, among others. Qualifications Master's degree in Nursing (MSN) required.\u00a0 Doctorate preferred (PhD, DNP, EdD) earned or in final semester/ABD with pending graduation date.\u00a0 Two (2) to three (3) years of leadership experience in nursing education administration required.\u00a0 Prior classroom and clinical teaching experience at the collegiate level required. Valid, unencumbered license as a registered nurse or advanced practice nurse in Pennsylvania required. Minimum 3-4 years of nursing experience, with at least two years in behavioral health nursing and a demonstrated ability to perform at a high level is required. A strong student focus is required, with the ability to relay information effectively.\u00a0 Excellent oral and written communication skills are expected.\u00a0 Proficiency with Microsoft Word and Excel is required. Must be able to work with minimal supervision and demonstrate the ability to prioritize, multitask, maintain attention to detail orientation, and excel in a fast-paced, high volume office.\u00a0 High degree of professionalism and a demonstrated ability to maintain high ethical standards and confidentiality is required. Proficiency in curriculum design, evaluation, instruction, program administration, and academic advising also preferred.\u00a0 Faculty rank is dependent upon education, experience and credentials. This role is not budgeted for visa sponsorship at this time; all candidates must be authorized to work in the US at the time of submission of their application. About Mount Aloysius College\u2019s Expansion into DuBois, PA Mount Aloysius College is bringing nursing education to DuBois beginning Fall 2026!\u00a0 Students can complete pre-nursing coursework this fall, and begin their path toward a rewarding healthcare career close to home with a two year associates degree. Through a new collaboration with Penn Highlands Healthcare, eligible nursing students may receive up to $48,000 in combined financial support, along with hands-on clinical opportunities and pathways to employment after graduation. Commitment to Diversity Mount Aloysius is committed to building an inclusive community that values each person and respects diversity of all kinds \u2013 diversity of thought, experience, culture, ethnicity, religion, gender/gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, etc. to create a workplace where everyone participates and is able to contribute their own unique gifts, talents and perspectives. Application Instructions Apply online at http://www.mtaloy.edu/employment-opportunities.\u00a0 All applicants should submit a resume with an accompanying cover letter.\u00a0 Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled.\u00a0 Applicants needing reasonable accommodation to participate in the application process should contact the Office of Human Resources at (814) 886-6519. Mount Aloysius College is an Equal Opportunity Employer Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by REQUIRED NOTICES The Mount Aloysius College Annual Security and Fire Safety Report contains statistics for the three previous calendar years of reported crimes that occurred on our campuses, in certain off-campus buildings or properties owned or controlled by Mount Aloysius College, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from our campuses. This annual report is required by federal law, and contains information regarding campus security and personal safety, including institutional policies, crime prevention, crime reporting policies, and fire safety. The report also includes our current Sexual Assault and Misconduct Policies. The 2024 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online. You may also request a printed copy from Mount Aloysius College's Office of Campus Safety, located in Ihmsen Hall 112, by calling (814) 886-6327 or via email to CampusSafety@mtaloy.edu EEO is the LAW Mount Aloysius College is an equal opportunity employer, and does not tolerate unlawful discrimination against any person on the basis of age, ancestry, color, disability or handicap, national origin, race, religious creed, gender, sexual orientation, genetic information or veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact us at 814-886-6500 or by email at HumanResources@mtaloy.edu. Employment will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with College policy. Mount Aloysius College"}, "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d098156f9c01982e34a60801d2&id=8a78839fa14d56d401a155150bb334ce&source=&lang=en": {"title": "Administrative Coordinator - School of Health Sciences", "description": "Careers | Mount Aloysius College Home Position: Administrative Coordinator - School of Health Sciences Location: Cresson, PA Job Id: 248 # of Openings: 1 Current Opening Mount Aloysius College, repeatedly recognized by ModernThink as a \u201cGreat College to Work For,\u201d\u00a0invites applications for a full-time Administrative Coordinator for the School of Health Sciences.\u00a0 This position\u00a0 provides direct administrative support to the\u00a0Dean of the School of Business, Arts, and Sciences\u00a0& Health Sciences, as well as additional support for Department Chairs, Clinical Coordinators, and Division Faculty. In the Administrative Coordinator capacity, the successful candidate serves as the main point of contact for all programs within the School of Health Sciences, which include Medical Imaging and Radiological Sciences, Physical Therapist Assistant, Science and Mathematics, Surgical Technology, and Ultrasonography.\u00a0 The Administrative Coordinator receives telephone, email, and in-person inquiries and directs callers/visitors as appropriate.\u00a0 Responsible for the preparation of correspondence, reports, and other documents, including official student notices, meeting minutes, programmatic accreditation preparation, etc.\u00a0 Responsible for accurate data coordination and data entry for the School of Health Sciences; maintains electronic records of important documents in a neat and organized manner.\u00a0 Coordinates timely management, completion and renewal of affiliation agreements with local healthcare organizations and other agencies; schedules meetings as directed; proctors make-up and licensing exams on an as-needed basis. The Administrative Coordinator also assists with preparation and implementation of various events hosted by the School of Health Sciences each year. Also, in this position, the successful candidate supports the Medical Imaging and Ultrasonography departments and their respective clinical coordinators in the clinical placement of students.\u00a0 To fulfill this responsibility, the Coordinator conducts outreach with existing and potential partners to provide clinical experiences for students, facilitates the acquisition of Clinical Education Agreements, prepares and delivers placement letters and reports, and maintains current and well-organized documentation.\u00a0 The Coordinator also manages the health screening process for students\u2019 placement in required clinical rotations in the Medical Imaging and Ultrasonography departments.\u00a0 To meet this requirement, the Coordinator ensures student health screenings are complete and up-to-date, verifies that records are uploaded in a timely manner, maintains detailed records of facility requirements, and manages dosimeters for the Medical Imaging department. Qualifications Associate Degree in secretarial/office administration or equivalent required.\u00a0 Three (3) years of administrative/secretarial support experience required.\u00a0 Professional work experience in the higher education setting is a plus.\u00a0 A strong customer service focus is required, with the ability to effectively relay information via telephone and email communications.\u00a0 Excellent oral and written communication skills are expected, as well as computer skills, including the ability to learn and effectively utilize the Jenzabar system.\u00a0 Proficiency in Microsoft Word and Excel required; advanced skill in creating Excel spreadsheets also required.\u00a0 Must be able to work under minimal supervision and demonstrate ability to prioritize, develop and manage workflow processes, and complete responsibilities in an organized and timely manner.\u00a0 High degree of professionalism and a demonstrated ability to maintain high ethical standards and confidentiality is required. This is a full-time, 12-month, benefit-eligible position. While some flexibility in scheduling and the opportunity for periodic remote days exists, this position is on campus in Cresson, PA, and is not eligible for remote work. This role is not budgeted for visa sponsorship at this time; all candidates must be authorized to work in the US at the time of submission of their application. About Mount Aloysius College Mount Aloysius College (www.mtaloy.edu) is a private, comprehensive Catholic college located in Pennsylvania\u2019s Laurel Highlands, serving a diverse community of learners. The College has a long history of responding to community needs through relevant academic programs and community service. Mount Aloysius is located on a 193-acre campus in Cresson, PA, Cambria County. Founded in 1853 by the Dublin, Ireland-based Religious Sisters of Mercy, Mount Aloysius is one of 17 such institutions in the United States and is a member of the Conference for Mercy Higher Education (CMHE). The College provides small class sizes, and students benefit from a highly engaged faculty and staff. Commitment to Diversity Mount Aloysius is committed to building an inclusive community that values each person and respects diversity of all kinds \u2013 diversity of thought, experience, culture, ethnicity, religion, gender/gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, etc. to create a workplace where everyone participates and is able to contribute their own unique gifts, talents and perspectives. Application Instructions Apply online at http://www.mtaloy.edu/employment-opportunities.\u00a0 All applicants should submit a resume with an accompanying cover letter.\u00a0 Applicants needing reasonable accommodation to participate in the application process should contact the Office of Human Resources at (814) 886-6519. Mount Aloysius College is an Equal Opportunity Employer Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by REQUIRED NOTICES The Mount Aloysius College Annual Security and Fire Safety Report contains statistics for the three previous calendar years of reported crimes that occurred on our campuses, in certain off-campus buildings or properties owned or controlled by Mount Aloysius College, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from our campuses. This annual report is required by federal law, and contains information regarding campus security and personal safety, including institutional policies, crime prevention, crime reporting policies, and fire safety. The report also includes our current Sexual Assault and Misconduct Policies. The 2024 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online. You may also request a printed copy from Mount Aloysius College's Office of Campus Safety, located in Ihmsen Hall 112, by calling (814) 886-6327 or via email to CampusSafety@mtaloy.edu EEO is the LAW Mount Aloysius College is an equal opportunity employer, and does not tolerate unlawful discrimination against any person on the basis of age, ancestry, color, disability or handicap, national origin, race, religious creed, gender, sexual orientation, genetic information or veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact us at 814-886-6500 or by email at HumanResources@mtaloy.edu. Employment will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with College policy. Mount Aloysius College"}, "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d098156f9c01982e34a60801d2&id=8a78859fa0f425c801a11bda7ff22187&source=&lang=en": {"title": "Director of Annual Giving & Alumni Relations", "description": "Careers | Mount Aloysius College Home Position: Director of Annual Giving & Alumni Relations Location: Cresson, PA Job Id: 245 # of Openings: 1 Current Opening Mount Aloysius College, repeatedly recognized by ModernThink as a \u201cGreat College to Work For,\u201d invites applications to join our Advancement & Engagement team as a full-time, year-round Director of Annual Giving & Alumni Relations. The Director of Annual Giving and Alumni Relations provides strategic leadership for the College\u2019s annual giving and alumni engagement programs, with responsibility for building lifelong relationships between Mount Aloysius College and its alumni, parents, families, friends, and other members of the College Community. This position develops and executes comprehensive annual giving strategies designed to increase donor acquisition, participation, retention, and philanthropic support.\u00a0 The Director leads alumni engagement initiatives that strengthen connections to the College and create meaningful opportunities for alumni to remain involved, informed, and invested in the institution. Working collaboratively across the Advancement and Engagement Department, the Director will use data, personal engagement, digital and traditional communications, events, and volunteer leadership to develop a sustainable pipeline of donors and advocates.\u00a0 The position will also identify opportunities to transition annual donors and engaged alumni into deeper philanthropic relationships with the College. The Director of Annual Giving & Alumni Relations is a non-voting ex-officio member of the Alumni Association Executive Board of Directors; and provides leadership and support to the Alumni Association in collaboration with the Executive Board. Advancement & Engagement at Mount Aloysius College is a comprehensive advancement services enterprise comprised of development/fundraising, alumni relations, grant writing & research, and related communications and events.\u00a0 Our team\u2019s mission is to build strong, lifelong relationships with Mount Aloysius College's constituents, match donors' interests with College\u2019s needs and priorities, and secure the financial resources necessary to support the Mission of the College. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor\u2019s degree required; Master\u2019s degree preferred.\u00a0 Five (5) to seven (7) years of progressively responsible administrative experience leading teams and managing complex projects or events required.\u00a0 Experience in higher education, fundraising, and working with volunteers is a plus.\u00a0 Excellent verbal, written, interpersonal, organizational, and listening skills required, and the ability to build and foster relationships across a diverse spectrum of individuals is a must.\u00a0 Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite and Google Suite required. Experience with Raiser\u2019s Edge database is a plus.\u00a0 Periodic work on evenings and weekends is required.\u00a0 High degree of professionalism and a demonstrated ability to maintain high ethical standards and confidentiality is required. This role is not budgeted for visa sponsorship at this time; all candidates must be authorized to work in the US at the time of submission of their application. About Mount Aloysius College Mount Aloysius College (www.mtaloy.edu) is a private, comprehensive Catholic college located in Pennsylvania\u2019s Laurel Highlands, serving a diverse community of learners. The College has a long history of responding to community needs through relevant academic programs and community service. Mount Aloysius is located on a 193-acre campus in Cresson, PA, Cambria County. Founded in 1853 by the Dublin, Ireland-based Religious Sisters of Mercy, Mount Aloysius is one of 17 such institutions in the United States and is a member of the Conference for Mercy Higher Education (CMHE). The College provides small class sizes, and students benefit from a highly engaged faculty and staff. Commitment to Diversity Mount Aloysius is committed to building an inclusive community that values each person and respects diversity of all kinds \u2013 diversity of thought, experience, culture, ethnicity, religion, gender/gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, etc. to create a workplace where everyone participates and is able to contribute their own unique gifts, talents and perspectives. Application Instructions Apply online at http://www.mtaloy.edu/employment-opportunities.\u00a0 All applicants should submit a resume with an accompanying cover letter.\u00a0 Applicants needing reasonable accommodation to participate in the application process should contact the Office of Human Resources at (814) 886-6519. Mount Aloysius College is an Equal Opportunity Employer Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by REQUIRED NOTICES The Mount Aloysius College Annual Security and Fire Safety Report contains statistics for the three previous calendar years of reported crimes that occurred on our campuses, in certain off-campus buildings or properties owned or controlled by Mount Aloysius College, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from our campuses. This annual report is required by federal law, and contains information regarding campus security and personal safety, including institutional policies, crime prevention, crime reporting policies, and fire safety. The report also includes our current Sexual Assault and Misconduct Policies. The 2024 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online. You may also request a printed copy from Mount Aloysius College's Office of Campus Safety, located in Ihmsen Hall 112, by calling (814) 886-6327 or via email to CampusSafety@mtaloy.edu EEO is the LAW Mount Aloysius College is an equal opportunity employer, and does not tolerate unlawful discrimination against any person on the basis of age, ancestry, color, disability or handicap, national origin, race, religious creed, gender, sexual orientation, genetic information or veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact us at 814-886-6500 or by email at HumanResources@mtaloy.edu. Employment will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with College policy. Mount Aloysius College"}, "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d098156f9c01982e34a60801d2&id=8a78859fa0f425c801a11cc8abd1039a&source=&lang=en": {"title": "Case Manager - Student Health & Wellness", "description": "Careers | Mount Aloysius College Home Position: Case Manager - Student Health & Wellness Location: Cresson, PA Job Id: 246 # of Openings: 1 Mount Aloysius College, repeatedly recognized by ModernThink as a \u201cGreat College to Work For,\u201d invites applications from student-centered individuals to join our Student Health & Wellness Team as the Case Manager.\u00a0 This position is a 10-month appointment, available at the start of the Spring 2027 semester.\u00a0 The Case Manager position runs from mid-August through mid-May and requires an additional 20 working days during the summer. Current Opening Reporting to the Director of Student Health & Wellness, the Case Manager provides goal-oriented, strength-based support to students experiencing academic, personal, medical, or other challenges that may create barriers to their success. The position assesses student needs, coordinates individualized action plans and referrals, connects students with campus and community resources, and provides ongoing follow-up to promote student persistence, well-being, and success. The Case Manager works collaboratively across Student Health & Wellness, Student Success and Persistence, and with other campus partners to provide coordinated support and an appropriate institutional response to students experiencing varying levels of distress. The Case Manager researches and identifies appropriate resources to address student needs and connects students with relevant on- and off-campus support services. Coordinates and monitors action plans, referrals, and support services, including follow-up appointments as necessary.\u00a0 The Case Manager documents case notes accurately and timely in the electronic record-keeping system and communicates and collaborates professionally with all individuals involved in supporting the student. The Case Manager coordinates with the Student Health and Wellness Department on outreach and programming initiatives, and participates in assessment efforts to evaluate the effectiveness of case management services. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor's degree in social work, student affairs, psychology, student development, or other related field degree.\u00a0 Experience providing support and assistance to individuals experiencing crisis or distress, as well as managing caseloads and coordinating ongoing support required.\u00a0 Strong working knowledge of mental health services, student development, Behavioral Intervention Team (BIT) best practices, higher education law, FERPA, and electronic record-keeping systems preferred.\u00a0 Prior experience working in the higher education setting is a plus. The successful candidate will demonstrate a student-centered, compassionate, and strengths-based approach to supporting students.\u00a0 Effective assessment, problem-solving, and resource coordination skills are essential to this position. Strong organizational,\u00a0 interpersonal, communication, coaching, and conflict-resolution skills are also necessary. The successful candidate must be able to establish trusting relationships while maintaining appropriate professional boundaries, as well as recognize when a student requires additional intervention, support, or referral. Demonstrated ability to prioritize, multitask, maintain attention to detail orientation, and excel in a fast-paced, high volume office.\u00a0 Must be able to work collaboratively across internal departments and with external community resources, and also exercise independent thinking.\u00a0 Should be able to foresee risks and anticipate needs, and make sound decisions.\u00a0 Ability to quickly and efficiently learn software that is highly utilized within the collegiate Student Health & Wellness space required.\u00a0 High degree of professionalism and a demonstrated ability to maintain high ethical standards and confidentiality is required.\u00a0 The successful candidate should be committed to supporting the holistic well-being, persistence, and success of our diverse student population. This is a full-time, 10-month, benefit-eligible position. While some flexibility in scheduling and the opportunity for periodic remote days exists, this position is on campus in Cresson, PA, and is not eligible for remote work. This role is not budgeted for visa sponsorship at this time; all candidates must be authorized to work in the US at the time of submission of their application. About Mount Aloysius College Mount Aloysius College (www.mtaloy.edu) is a private, comprehensive Catholic college located in Pennsylvania\u2019s Laurel Highlands, serving a diverse community of learners. The College has a long history of responding to community needs through relevant academic programs and community service. Mount Aloysius is located on a 193-acre campus in Cresson, PA, Cambria County. Founded in 1853 by the Dublin, Ireland-based Religious Sisters of Mercy, Mount Aloysius is one of 17 such institutions in the United States and is a member of the Conference for Mercy Higher Education (CMHE). The College provides small class sizes, and students benefit from a highly engaged faculty and staff. Commitment to Diversity Mount Aloysius is committed to building an inclusive community that values each person and respects diversity of all kinds \u2013 diversity of thought, experience, culture, ethnicity, religion, gender/gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, etc. to create a workplace where everyone participates and is able to contribute their own unique gifts, talents and perspectives. Application Instructions Apply online at http://www.mtaloy.edu/employment-opportunities.\u00a0 All applicants should submit a resume with an accompanying cover letter.\u00a0 Applicants needing reasonable accommodation to participate in the application process should contact the Office of Human Resources at (814) 886-6519. Mount Aloysius College is an Equal Opportunity Employer Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by REQUIRED NOTICES The Mount Aloysius College Annual Security and Fire Safety Report contains statistics for the three previous calendar years of reported crimes that occurred on our campuses, in certain off-campus buildings or properties owned or controlled by Mount Aloysius College, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from our campuses. This annual report is required by federal law, and contains information regarding campus security and personal safety, including institutional policies, crime prevention, crime reporting policies, and fire safety. The report also includes our current Sexual Assault and Misconduct Policies. The 2024 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online. You may also request a printed copy from Mount Aloysius College's Office of Campus Safety, located in Ihmsen Hall 112, by calling (814) 886-6327 or via email to CampusSafety@mtaloy.edu EEO is the LAW Mount Aloysius College is an equal opportunity employer, and does not tolerate unlawful discrimination against any person on the basis of age, ancestry, color, disability or handicap, national origin, race, religious creed, gender, sexual orientation, genetic information or veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact us at 814-886-6500 or by email at HumanResources@mtaloy.edu. Employment will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with College policy. Mount Aloysius College"}, "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d098156f9c01982e34a60801d2&id=8a7885a8a13c11b801a145b819c44034&source=&lang=en": {"title": "Professional Tutor - DuBois", "description": "Careers | Mount Aloysius College Home Position: Professional Tutor - DuBois Location: DuBois, PA Job Id: 247 # of Openings: 1 Mount Aloysius College, repeatedly recognized by ModernThink as a \u201cGreat College to Work For,\u201d invites applications from highly qualified registered nurses to join our team of educators as a Professional Tutor for students in the Nursing, Surgical Technology, and Radiography/Medical Imaging programs at our DuBois location.\u00a0 This position is a 9-month appointment, available at the start of the Spring 2027 semester. Current Opening The Professional Tutor is responsible for providing individual and group tutoring sessions for students requiring assistance with coursework in the Nursing, Surgical Technology, and Radiography/Medical Imaging programs. This may include individual and small group tutorial sessions on topics that correlate with classroom studies. Additionally, the Professional Tutor meets regularly with faculty for assigned courses to coordinate tutoring efforts and communicate student needs and academic progress. Some evening and weekend hours are required. Qualifications Valid, unencumbered PA RN license required.\u00a0 Bachelor\u2019s Degree in Nursing (BSN) required.\u00a0 Two years of experience as an educator or facilitating educational programs in a hospital, healthcare, or academic environment preferred.\u00a0 Master\u2019s degree with nurse educator experience preferred. Demonstrated ability to teach or explain complex topics within the Health Sciences, including but not limited to Nursing, Surgical Technology, and Radiography/Medical Imaging disciplines, as well as anatomy and physiology, microbiology, and chemistry required. Collegiate tutoring experience is strongly preferred. This role is not budgeted for visa sponsorship at this time; all candidates must be authorized to work in the US at the time of submission of their application. About Mount Aloysius College Mount Aloysius College (www.mtaloy.edu) is a private, comprehensive Catholic college located in Pennsylvania\u2019s Laurel Highlands, serving a diverse community of learners. The College has a long history of responding to community needs through relevant academic programs and community service. Mount Aloysius is located on a 193-acre campus in Cresson, PA, Cambria County. Founded in 1853 by the Dublin, Ireland-based Religious Sisters of Mercy, Mount Aloysius is one of 17 such institutions in the United States and is a member of the Conference for Mercy Higher Education (CMHE). The College provides small class sizes, and students benefit from a highly engaged faculty and staff. Commitment to Diversity Mount Aloysius is committed to building an inclusive community that values each person and respects diversity of all kinds \u2013 diversity of thought, experience, culture, ethnicity, religion, gender/gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, etc. to create a workplace where everyone participates and is able to contribute their own unique gifts, talents and perspectives. Application Instructions Apply online at http://www.mtaloy.edu/employment-opportunities.\u00a0 All applicants should submit a resume with an accompanying cover letter.\u00a0 Applicants needing reasonable accommodation to participate in the application process should contact the Office of Human Resources at (814) 886-6519. Mount Aloysius College is an Equal Opportunity Employer Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by REQUIRED NOTICES The Mount Aloysius College Annual Security and Fire Safety Report contains statistics for the three previous calendar years of reported crimes that occurred on our campuses, in certain off-campus buildings or properties owned or controlled by Mount Aloysius College, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from our campuses. This annual report is required by federal law, and contains information regarding campus security and personal safety, including institutional policies, crime prevention, crime reporting policies, and fire safety. The report also includes our current Sexual Assault and Misconduct Policies. The 2024 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online. You may also request a printed copy from Mount Aloysius College's Office of Campus Safety, located in Ihmsen Hall 112, by calling (814) 886-6327 or via email to CampusSafety@mtaloy.edu EEO is the LAW Mount Aloysius College is an equal opportunity employer, and does not tolerate unlawful discrimination against any person on the basis of age, ancestry, color, disability or handicap, national origin, race, religious creed, gender, sexual orientation, genetic information or veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact us at 814-886-6500 or by email at HumanResources@mtaloy.edu. Employment will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with College policy. Mount Aloysius College"}, "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d098156f9c01982e34a60801d2&id=8a7885aca03fc28401a0626ec38e046e&source=&lang=en": {"title": "Interim Clinical Coordinator - Ultrasonography (Temp, FT)", "description": "Careers | Mount Aloysius College Home Position: Interim Clinical Coordinator - Ultrasonography (Temp, FT) Location: Clinical Sites, PA Job Id: 230 # of Openings: 1 Mount Aloysius College, repeatedly recognized by ModernThink as a \u201cGreat College to Work For,\u201d invites applications from highly qualified individuals to join our team of faculty in the Ultrasonography Department for a temporary, full-time appointment as\u00a0Interim Clinical Coordinator,\u00a0beginning October 5, 2026 and ending in mid February, 2027. Current Opening This open position offers a temporary, full-time faculty appointment consisting of\u00a0 primary coordinator\u00a0and teaching obligations.\u00a0 Faculty are expected to have a regular presence on campus to engage with students both inside and outside the classroom.\u00a0 The successful candidate will be responsible for clinical coordination, teaching (labs and introductory theory courses as needed), and work related to students in the Ultrasonography Program.\u00a0 Candidate responsibilities will focus on coordination of clinical sites, but will also include instruction and evaluation of students and clinical affiliates.\u00a0 The successful candidate will be responsible for coordinating clinical education,\u00a0evaluate\u00a0and ensure the effectiveness of clinical experiences; and provide clinical instruction and document the evaluation and\u00a0progression of clinical performance leading to clinical competence. Qualifications Bachelor\u2019s degree in medical imaging field required; and must possess Ultrasound credentials in Abdominal, Breast\u00a0and OB/GYN.\u00a0Candidates who are credentialed in Adult Echocardiography, in addition to Abdominal, Breast, and OB/GYN, are also welcome to apply.\u00a0\u00a0Two (2) years of full-time sonography experience required as well. Teaching experience in the clinical setting preferred, especially ultrasound.\u00a0In addition, the successful candidate will possess excellent verbal, written, interpersonal and organizational skills; and be proficient in computer technology to include Microsoft Word and Excel. Demonstrated ability to multi-task and maintain confidentiality required. Reports to the\u00a0Ultrasonography Department Chairperson. Due to the temporary nature of this position, neither benefits nor paid holidays will be offered. This role is not budgeted for visa sponsorship at this time; all candidates must be authorized to work in the US at the time of submission of their application. About Mount Aloysius College Mount Aloysius College (www.mtaloy.edu) is a private, comprehensive Catholic college located in Pennsylvania\u2019s Laurel Highlands, serving a diverse community of learners. The College has a long history of responding to community needs through relevant academic programs and community service. Mount Aloysius is located on a 193-acre campus in Cresson, PA, Cambria County. Founded in 1853 by the Dublin, Ireland-based Religious Sisters of Mercy, Mount Aloysius is one of 17 such institutions in the United States and is a member of the Conference for Mercy Higher Education (CMHE). The College provides small class sizes, and students benefit from a highly engaged faculty and staff. Commitment to Diversity Mount Aloysius is committed to building an inclusive community that values each person and respects diversity of all kinds \u2013 diversity of thought, experience, culture, ethnicity, religion, gender/gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, etc. to create a workplace where everyone participates and is able to contribute their own unique gifts, talents and perspectives. Application Instructions Apply online at http://www.mtaloy.edu/employment-opportunities.\u00a0 All applicants should submit a resume with an accompanying cover letter.\u00a0 Applicants needing reasonable accommodation to participate in the application process should contact the Office of Human Resources at (814) 886-6519. Mount Aloysius College is an Equal Opportunity Employer Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by REQUIRED NOTICES The Mount Aloysius College Annual Security and Fire Safety Report contains statistics for the three previous calendar years of reported crimes that occurred on our campuses, in certain off-campus buildings or properties owned or controlled by Mount Aloysius College, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from our campuses. This annual report is required by federal law, and contains information regarding campus security and personal safety, including institutional policies, crime prevention, crime reporting policies, and fire safety. The report also includes our current Sexual Assault and Misconduct Policies. The 2024 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online. You may also request a printed copy from Mount Aloysius College's Office of Campus Safety, located in Ihmsen Hall 112, by calling (814) 886-6327 or via email to CampusSafety@mtaloy.edu EEO is the LAW Mount Aloysius College is an equal opportunity employer, and does not tolerate unlawful discrimination against any person on the basis of age, ancestry, color, disability or handicap, national origin, race, religious creed, gender, sexual orientation, genetic information or veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact us at 814-886-6500 or by email at HumanResources@mtaloy.edu. Employment will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with College policy. Mount Aloysius College"}, "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d098156f9c01982e34a60801d2&id=8a7885aca0abfc6901a0d55653017d22&source=&lang=en": {"title": "Interim Instructor - Ultrasonography (Temp, FT)", "description": "Careers | Mount Aloysius College Home Position: Interim Instructor - Ultrasonography (Temp, FT) Location: Cresson, PA Job Id: 241 # of Openings: 1 Mount Aloysius College, repeatedly recognized by ModernThink as a \u201cGreat College to Work For,\u201d invites applications from highly qualified individuals to join our team of faculty in the Ultrasonography Department for a temporary, full-time appointment as\u00a0Interim Instructor,\u00a0beginning October 5, 2026 and continuing through the end of the Spring 2027 semester. Current Opening This open position offers a temporary, full-time faculty appointment consisting of primary teaching obligations.\u00a0 Faculty are expected to have a regular presence on campus to engage with students both inside and outside the classroom.\u00a0 The successful candidate will be responsible for teaching (labs and introductory theory courses as needed), and work related to students in the Ultrasonography Program.\u00a0 Candidate responsibilities will include instruction and evaluation of students and completion of departmental duties/administrative tasks.\u00a0 The successful candidate will be responsible for coordinating clinical education,\u00a0evaluate\u00a0and ensure the effectiveness of clinical experiences; and provide clinical instruction and document the evaluation and\u00a0progression of clinical performance leading to clinical competence. This position is required to report to campus in Cresson, PA. Qualifications Bachelor\u2019s degree in medical imaging field required; and must possess Ultrasound credentials in Abdominal, Breast\u00a0and OB/GYN.\u00a0Candidates who are credentialed in Adult Echocardiography, in addition to Abdominal, Breast, and OB/GYN, are also welcome to apply.\u00a0\u00a0Two (2) years of full-time sonography experience required as well. Teaching experience in the clinical setting preferred, especially ultrasound.\u00a0In addition, the successful candidate will possess excellent verbal, written, interpersonal and organizational skills; and be proficient in computer technology to include Microsoft Word and Excel. Demonstrated ability to multi-task and maintain confidentiality required. Reports to the\u00a0Ultrasonography Department Chairperson. Due to the temporary nature of this position, neither benefits nor paid holidays will be offered. This role is not budgeted for visa sponsorship at this time; all candidates must be authorized to work in the US at the time of submission of their application. About Mount Aloysius College Mount Aloysius College (www.mtaloy.edu) is a private, comprehensive Catholic college located in Pennsylvania\u2019s Laurel Highlands, serving a diverse community of learners. The College has a long history of responding to community needs through relevant academic programs and community service. Mount Aloysius is located on a 193-acre campus in Cresson, PA, Cambria County. Founded in 1853 by the Dublin, Ireland-based Religious Sisters of Mercy, Mount Aloysius is one of 17 such institutions in the United States and is a member of the Conference for Mercy Higher Education (CMHE). The College provides small class sizes, and students benefit from a highly engaged faculty and staff. Commitment to Diversity Mount Aloysius is committed to building an inclusive community that values each person and respects diversity of all kinds \u2013 diversity of thought, experience, culture, ethnicity, religion, gender/gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, etc. to create a workplace where everyone participates and is able to contribute their own unique gifts, talents and perspectives. Application Instructions Apply online at http://www.mtaloy.edu/employment-opportunities.\u00a0 All applicants should submit a resume with an accompanying cover letter.\u00a0 Applicants needing reasonable accommodation to participate in the application process should contact the Office of Human Resources at (814) 886-6519. Mount Aloysius College is an Equal Opportunity Employer Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by REQUIRED NOTICES The Mount Aloysius College Annual Security and Fire Safety Report contains statistics for the three previous calendar years of reported crimes that occurred on our campuses, in certain off-campus buildings or properties owned or controlled by Mount Aloysius College, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from our campuses. This annual report is required by federal law, and contains information regarding campus security and personal safety, including institutional policies, crime prevention, crime reporting policies, and fire safety. The report also includes our current Sexual Assault and Misconduct Policies. The 2024 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online. You may also request a printed copy from Mount Aloysius College's Office of Campus Safety, located in Ihmsen Hall 112, by calling (814) 886-6327 or via email to CampusSafety@mtaloy.edu EEO is the LAW Mount Aloysius College is an equal opportunity employer, and does not tolerate unlawful discrimination against any person on the basis of age, ancestry, color, disability or handicap, national origin, race, religious creed, gender, sexual orientation, genetic information or veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact us at 814-886-6500 or by email at HumanResources@mtaloy.edu. Employment will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with College policy. Mount Aloysius College"}, "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d098156f9c01982e34a60801d2&id=8a78879ea06420fb01a0a5293d4133af&source=&lang=en": {"title": "Campus Safety Officer (Part-Time)", "description": "Careers | Mount Aloysius College Home Position: Campus Safety Officer (Part-Time) Location: Cresson, PA Job Id: 235 # of Openings: 1 Current Opening Mount Aloysius College, repeatedly recognized by ModernThink as a \u201cGreat College to Work For,\u201d is searching for qualified applicants from ACT 120 Certified Law Enforcement Officers to join our team of Police and Safety professionals as a Campus Safety Officer.\u00a0 Regular part-time opportunities are available. The Campus Safety\u00a0Department\u00a0provides a safe and secure learning and working environment for students, faculty, staff and visitors. Duties include but are not limited to: vehicular and foot patrols of campus buildings and grounds, event\u00a0parking and traffic control,\u00a0enforcement of criminal and traffic laws, as well as College promulgated rules and regulations, investigation of crimes, completion of police reports, and testifying in court.\u00a0Additionally, Officers are asked to assist with educational programming and to engage with students in positive and proactive ways. Safety related tasks will also be assigned and may include building inspections, smoke detector and fire extinguisher checks, among others. Minimum Qualifications Strong desire to work in a College environment is a must.\u00a0 High School Diploma or GED required. Act 120 Municipal Police Training or PA State Police Academy required. Three (3) years of law enforcement experience required, preferably in a College or University setting. Valid PA Driver's License and current CPR/AED certification required. Employment is contingent upon satisfactory completion of a psychological evaluation, criminal, child abuse, and FBI Fingerprinting clearances. This part-time position is not eligible for remote work or benefits.\u00a0 This role is not budgeted for visa sponsorship at this time; all candidates must be authorized to work in the US at the time of submission of their application. About Mount Aloysius College Mount Aloysius College (www.mtaloy.edu) is a private, comprehensive Catholic college located in Pennsylvania\u2019s Laurel Highlands, serving a diverse community of learners. The College has a long history of responding to community needs through relevant academic programs and community service. Mount Aloysius is located on a 193-acre campus in Cresson, PA, Cambria County. Founded in 1853 by the Dublin, Ireland-based Religious Sisters of Mercy, Mount Aloysius is one of 17 such institutions in the United States and is a member of the Conference for Mercy Higher Education (CMHE). The College provides small class sizes, and students benefit from a highly engaged faculty and staff. Commitment to Diversity Mount Aloysius is committed to building an inclusive community that values each person and respects diversity of all kinds \u2013 diversity of thought, experience, culture, ethnicity, religion, gender/gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, etc. to create a workplace where everyone participates and is able to contribute their own unique gifts, talents and perspectives. Application Instructions Apply online at\u00a0http://www.mtaloy.edu/employment-opportunities.\u00a0 Review of applicants will begin once a suitable candidate pool is identified and continue until the position is filled. Applicants needing reasonable accommodation to participate in the application process should contact the Office of Human Resources at (814) 886-6519. Mount Aloysius College is an Equal Opportunity Employer Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by REQUIRED NOTICES The Mount Aloysius College Annual Security and Fire Safety Report contains statistics for the three previous calendar years of reported crimes that occurred on our campuses, in certain off-campus buildings or properties owned or controlled by Mount Aloysius College, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from our campuses. This annual report is required by federal law, and contains information regarding campus security and personal safety, including institutional policies, crime prevention, crime reporting policies, and fire safety. The report also includes our current Sexual Assault and Misconduct Policies. The 2024 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online. You may also request a printed copy from Mount Aloysius College's Office of Campus Safety, located in Ihmsen Hall 112, by calling (814) 886-6327 or via email to CampusSafety@mtaloy.edu EEO is the LAW Mount Aloysius College is an equal opportunity employer, and does not tolerate unlawful discrimination against any person on the basis of age, ancestry, color, disability or handicap, national origin, race, religious creed, gender, sexual orientation, genetic information or veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact us at 814-886-6500 or by email at HumanResources@mtaloy.edu. Employment will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with College policy. Mount Aloysius College"}, "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d098156f9c01982e34a60801d2&id=8a78879ea06420fb01a0a580b1b35743&source=&lang=en": {"title": "Campus Safety Officer (Full-Time)", "description": "Careers | Mount Aloysius College Home Position: Campus Safety Officer (Full-Time) Location: Cresson, PA Job Id: 236 # of Openings: 1 Current Opening Mount Aloysius College, repeatedly recognized by ModernThink as a \u201cGreat College to Work For,\u201d is searching for qualified applicants from ACT 120 Certified Law Enforcement Officers to join our team of Police and Safety professionals as a Campus Safety Officer.\u00a0 Regular full-time opportunities are available.\u00a0 The successful candidate will have the overnight shift option of 3:00 pm to 1:00 am or 2:00 pm to 12:00 am. The Campus Safety\u00a0Department\u00a0provides a safe and secure learning and working environment for students, faculty, staff and visitors. Duties include but are not limited to: vehicular and foot patrols of campus buildings and grounds, event\u00a0parking and traffic control,\u00a0enforcement of criminal and traffic laws, as well as College promulgated rules and regulations, investigation of crimes, completion of police reports, and testifying in court.\u00a0Additionally, Officers are asked to assist with educational programming and to engage with students in positive and proactive ways. Safety related tasks will also be assigned and may include building inspections, smoke detector and fire extinguisher checks, among others. Minimum Qualifications Strong desire to work in a College environment is a must.\u00a0 High School Diploma or GED required. Act 120 Municipal Police Training or PA State Police Academy required. Three (3) years of law enforcement experience required, preferably in a College or University setting. Valid PA Driver's License and current CPR/AED certification required. Employment is contingent upon satisfactory completion of a psychological evaluation, criminal, child abuse, and FBI Fingerprinting clearances. This role is not budgeted for visa sponsorship at this time; all candidates must be authorized to work in the US at the time of submission of their application. About Mount Aloysius College Mount Aloysius College (www.mtaloy.edu) is a private, comprehensive Catholic college located in Pennsylvania\u2019s Laurel Highlands, serving a diverse community of learners. The College has a long history of responding to community needs through relevant academic programs and community service. Mount Aloysius is located on a 193-acre campus in Cresson, PA, Cambria County. Founded in 1853 by the Dublin, Ireland-based Religious Sisters of Mercy, Mount Aloysius is one of 17 such institutions in the United States and is a member of the Conference for Mercy Higher Education (CMHE). The College provides small class sizes, and students benefit from a highly engaged faculty and staff. Commitment to Diversity Mount Aloysius is committed to building an inclusive community that values each person and respects diversity of all kinds \u2013 diversity of thought, experience, culture, ethnicity, religion, gender/gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, etc. to create a workplace where everyone participates and is able to contribute their own unique gifts, talents and perspectives. Application Instructions Apply online at\u00a0http://www.mtaloy.edu/employment-opportunities.\u00a0 Review of applicants will begin once a suitable candidate pool is identified and continue until the position is filled. Applicants needing reasonable accommodation to participate in the application process should contact the Office of Human Resources at (814) 886-6519. Mount Aloysius College is an Equal Opportunity Employer Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by REQUIRED NOTICES The Mount Aloysius College Annual Security and Fire Safety Report contains statistics for the three previous calendar years of reported crimes that occurred on our campuses, in certain off-campus buildings or properties owned or controlled by Mount Aloysius College, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from our campuses. This annual report is required by federal law, and contains information regarding campus security and personal safety, including institutional policies, crime prevention, crime reporting policies, and fire safety. The report also includes our current Sexual Assault and Misconduct Policies. The 2024 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online. You may also request a printed copy from Mount Aloysius College's Office of Campus Safety, located in Ihmsen Hall 112, by calling (814) 886-6327 or via email to CampusSafety@mtaloy.edu EEO is the LAW Mount Aloysius College is an equal opportunity employer, and does not tolerate unlawful discrimination against any person on the basis of age, ancestry, color, disability or handicap, national origin, race, religious creed, gender, sexual orientation, genetic information or veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact us at 814-886-6500 or by email at HumanResources@mtaloy.edu. Employment will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with College policy. Mount Aloysius College"}, "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d098156f9c01982e34a60801d2&id=8a7887a19de07068019e1d44dd9c4929&source=&lang=en": {"title": "Adjunct Faculty (Clinical) - Nursing", "description": "Careers | Mount Aloysius College Home Position: Adjunct Faculty (Clinical) - Nursing Location: Clinical Sites, PA Job Id: 219 # of Openings: 1 Current Opening Mount Aloysius College, repeatedly recognized by ModernThink as a \u201cGreat College to Work For,\u201d seeks qualified registered nurses for adjunct clinical teaching opportunities in Medical-Surgical Nursing across all levels, including Intensive Care, during the upcoming Fall 2026 semester. Adjunct faculty at Mount Aloysius College may participate in our retirement savings plan, and are eligible for limited tuition remission benefits for themselves and their dependents.\u00a0 As an Adjunct faculty member, you also receive complimentary access to our wellness center/gym, are eligible for the Employee Assistance Program (EAP) and have access to various employee discounts. Qualifications Minimum 3 years of clinical experience in Medical-Surgical Nursing required. Valid PA RN license also required. BSN required; MSN preferred. If currently BSN prepared, candidate must be willing to enroll in a Master\u2019s Degree in Nursing program. Per Pennsylvania State Board of Nursing, faculty with a BSN will need to provide evidence of a plan to obtain a graduate degree in nursing. In Pennsylvania, a person may teach in a nursing education program with a BSN for a maximum cumulative period of 5 years. Successful candidate/s will be required to submit documentation of various clearances upon hire. About Mount Aloysius College Mount Aloysius College (www.mtaloy.edu) is a private, comprehensive Catholic college located in Pennsylvania\u2019s Laurel Highlands, serving a diverse community of learners. The College has a long history of responding to community needs through relevant academic programs and community service. Mount Aloysius is located on a 193-acre campus in Cresson, PA, Cambria County. Founded in 1853 by the Dublin, Ireland-based Religious Sisters of Mercy, Mount Aloysius is one of 17 such institutions in the United States and is a member of the Conference for Mercy Higher Education (CMHE). The College provides small class sizes, and students benefit from a highly engaged faculty and staff. Commitment to Diversity Mount Aloysius is committed to building an inclusive community that values each person and respects diversity of all kinds \u2013 diversity of thought, experience, culture, ethnicity, religion, gender/gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, etc. to create a workplace where everyone participates and is able to contribute their own unique gifts, talents and perspectives. Application Instructions Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. All applicants should submit a resume with accompanying cover letter and three professional references. Applicants needing reasonable accommodation to participate in the application process should contact the Office of Human Resources at (814) 886-6519. Mount Aloysius College is an Equal Opportunity Employer Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by REQUIRED NOTICES The Mount Aloysius College Annual Security and Fire Safety Report contains statistics for the three previous calendar years of reported crimes that occurred on our campuses, in certain off-campus buildings or properties owned or controlled by Mount Aloysius College, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from our campuses. This annual report is required by federal law, and contains information regarding campus security and personal safety, including institutional policies, crime prevention, crime reporting policies, and fire safety. The report also includes our current Sexual Assault and Misconduct Policies. The 2024 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online. You may also request a printed copy from Mount Aloysius College's Office of Campus Safety, located in Ihmsen Hall 112, by calling (814) 886-6327 or via email to CampusSafety@mtaloy.edu EEO is the LAW Mount Aloysius College is an equal opportunity employer, and does not tolerate unlawful discrimination against any person on the basis of age, ancestry, color, disability or handicap, national origin, race, religious creed, gender, sexual orientation, genetic information or veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact us at 814-886-6500 or by email at HumanResources@mtaloy.edu. Employment will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with College policy. Mount Aloysius College"}, "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d098156f9c01982e34a60801d2&id=8a7887a1a064211201a06da3ccc6030d&source=&lang=en": {"title": "Housekeeper", "description": "Careers | Mount Aloysius College Home Position: Housekeeper Location: Cresson, PA Job Id: 232 # of Openings: 1 Mount Aloysius College, repeatedly recognized by ModernThink as a \u201cGreat College to Work For,\u201d\u00a0is seeking applications for a full-time Housekeeper. Current Opening The Housekeeper is responsible for maintaining the cleanliness of College buildings, including classrooms, offices, lounges, restrooms, hallways, and other public or common areas.\u00a0 Cleaning duties include but are not limited to vacuuming, sweeping, mopping, dusting, and periodically scrubbing floors, washing windows, and shampooing carpets. Qualifications High School Diploma or General Education Degree (GED) required.\u00a0 Experience in housekeeping/custodial desirable.\u00a0\u00a0Ability to carry out assigned responsibilities independently in the absence of direct supervision and follow oral and/or written directions required. Ability to set work priorities and establish positive rapport with coworkers also required.\u00a0 Shift/s will be determined based on coverage needs. This position requires occasional evening and weekend hours to assist with special events.\u00a0 Background clearances including FBI Fingerprint, criminal history and PA child abuse required. This is a full-time, 12-month, benefit-eligible position.\u00a0 This role is not budgeted for visa sponsorship at this time; all candidates must be authorized to work in the US at the time of submission of their application. About Mount Aloysius College Mount Aloysius College (www.mtaloy.edu) is a private, comprehensive Catholic college located in Pennsylvania\u2019s Laurel Highlands, serving a diverse community of learners. The College has a long history of responding to community needs through relevant academic programs and community service. Mount Aloysius is located on a 193-acre campus in Cresson, PA, Cambria County. Founded in 1853 by the Dublin, Ireland-based Religious Sisters of Mercy, Mount Aloysius is one of 17 such institutions in the United States and is a member of the Conference for Mercy Higher Education (CMHE). The College provides small class sizes, and students benefit from a highly engaged faculty and staff. Commitment to Diversity Mount Aloysius is committed to building an inclusive community that values each person and respects diversity of all kinds \u2013 diversity of thought, experience, culture, ethnicity, religion, gender/gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, etc. to create a workplace where everyone participates and is able to contribute their own unique gifts, talents and perspectives. Application Instructions Apply online at http://www.mtaloy.edu/employment-opportunities.\u00a0 All applicants should submit a resume with an accompanying cover letter.\u00a0 Applicants needing reasonable accommodation to participate in the application process should contact the Office of Human Resources at (814) 886-6519. Mount Aloysius College is an Equal Opportunity Employer Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by REQUIRED NOTICES The Mount Aloysius College Annual Security and Fire Safety Report contains statistics for the three previous calendar years of reported crimes that occurred on our campuses, in certain off-campus buildings or properties owned or controlled by Mount Aloysius College, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from our campuses. This annual report is required by federal law, and contains information regarding campus security and personal safety, including institutional policies, crime prevention, crime reporting policies, and fire safety. The report also includes our current Sexual Assault and Misconduct Policies. The 2024 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online. You may also request a printed copy from Mount Aloysius College's Office of Campus Safety, located in Ihmsen Hall 112, by calling (814) 886-6327 or via email to CampusSafety@mtaloy.edu EEO is the LAW Mount Aloysius College is an equal opportunity employer, and does not tolerate unlawful discrimination against any person on the basis of age, ancestry, color, disability or handicap, national origin, race, religious creed, gender, sexual orientation, genetic information or veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact us at 814-886-6500 or by email at HumanResources@mtaloy.edu. Employment will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with College policy. Mount Aloysius College"}, "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d098156f9c01982e34a60801d2&id=8a7887a8a0abfc8001a0ce84b40e66e2&source=&lang=en": {"title": "Head Coach - Men's & Women's Wrestling", "description": "Careers | Mount Aloysius College Home Position: Head Coach - Men's & Women's Wrestling Location: Cresson, PA Job Id: 240 # of Openings: 1 Current Opening Mount Aloysius College, repeatedly recognized by ModernThink as a \u201cGreat College to Work For,\u201d invites applications for an ambitious coach and leader to join our NCAA Division III Athletics Program as\u00a0its inaugural Head Coach for Men\u2019s & Women\u2019s Wrestling.\u00a0 This full-time, year-round coaching position (available for hire beginning Fall 2026) presents the new incumbent with a unique opportunity to build and develop a Men\u2019s and Women\u2019s Wrestling program, beginning competition during the 2027-2028 academic year. The Head Coach is tasked with establishing a solid foundation and ensuring growth and development of the Men\u2019s & Women\u2019s Wrestling program through effective strategies and planning that promote and sustain\u00a0 the program.\u00a0 The Head Coach will plan/direct the activities of the Men\u2019s & Women\u2019s Wrestling teams and is directly responsible for the recruitment and retention of student athletes.\u00a0 It is expected that the Head Coach will meet or exceed annual recruitment goals established in collaboration with the VP for Athletics & Community Outreach.\u00a0 Supports overall athletic recruiting efforts at the College, and may recruit for other sports as deemed appropriate by the VP for Athletics & Community Outreach. The Head Coach will guide and oversee conditioning of student athletes, instruct student athletes in techniques of the sport, assess student athletes\u2019 skills, evaluate own and opposing team capabilities, promote camaraderie and instill good sportsmanship.\u00a0 The Head Coach performs other administrative duties as assigned in support of the\u00a0Department of Athletics\u00a0(game\u00a0management, recruiting, etc.) and collaborates with other coaching staff to support College and department goals and objectives.\u00a0\u00a0Oversees Assistant Coach(es) or Graduate Assistant as may be assigned.\u00a0 In the spirit of our Mercy heritage and traditions, the Head Coach plans and leads at least one Community service initiative for the Wrestling teams annually.\u00a0 The Head Coach is expected to actively engage with the Mount Aloysius College community and maintain an established network to advance the development of the Men\u2019s & Women\u2019s Wrestling program. As a DIII Institution, Mount Aloysius emphasizes the importance of academics and expects coaching staff to monitor student athletes\u2019 academic progress.\u00a0 The Head Coach is responsible to comply with NCAA Division III and Allegheny Mountain Collegiate Conference regulations; and is subject to NCAA enforcement provisions for violations. Qualifications Bachelor\u2019s Degree required.\u00a0 Minimum of three (3) years coaching experience as an assistant coach or high school head coach required, or equivalent combination of coaching and playing experience.\u00a0 Must be knowledgeable of NCAA Division III philosophy, rules and regulations pertaining to men\u2019s and women\u2019s wrestling. Excellent interpersonal and organizational skills required.\u00a0\u00a0Ability to\u00a0communicate\u00a0effectively with colleagues, student athletes, recruits, and stakeholders\u00a0 a must.\u00a0 Ability to motivate and lead student athletes individually and in a team setting also required.\u00a0 Ability to work independently and as a team member\u00a0is highly valued.\u00a0 Must be available to work a flexible schedule, including weekends, evenings, and some holidays required.\u00a0 Travel and occasional overnight stays expected for games and recruiting. This is a full-time, 12-month, benefit eligible position.\u00a0 This position is on campus in Cresson, PA and is not eligible for remote work.\u00a0 This role is not budgeted for visa sponsorship at this time; all candidates must be authorized to work in the US at the time of submission of their application. About Mount Aloysius College Mount Aloysius College (www.mtaloy.edu) is a private, comprehensive Catholic college located in Pennsylvania\u2019s Laurel Highlands, serving a diverse community of learners. The College has a long history of responding to community needs through relevant academic programs and community service. Mount Aloysius is located on a 193-acre campus in Cresson, PA, Cambria County. Founded in 1853 by the Dublin, Ireland-based Religious Sisters of Mercy, Mount Aloysius is one of 17 such institutions in the United States and is a member of the Conference for Mercy Higher Education (CMHE). The College provides small class sizes, and students benefit from a highly engaged faculty and staff. Application Instructions Apply online at http://www.mtaloy.edu/employment-opportunities.\u00a0 All applicants should submit a resume with an accompanying cover letter.\u00a0 Applicants needing reasonable accommodation to participate in the application process should contact the Office of Human Resources at (814) 886-6519. Mount Aloysius College is an Equal Opportunity Employer Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by REQUIRED NOTICES The Mount Aloysius College Annual Security and Fire Safety Report contains statistics for the three previous calendar years of reported crimes that occurred on our campuses, in certain off-campus buildings or properties owned or controlled by Mount Aloysius College, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from our campuses. This annual report is required by federal law, and contains information regarding campus security and personal safety, including institutional policies, crime prevention, crime reporting policies, and fire safety. The report also includes our current Sexual Assault and Misconduct Policies. The 2024 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online. You may also request a printed copy from Mount Aloysius College's Office of Campus Safety, located in Ihmsen Hall 112, by calling (814) 886-6327 or via email to CampusSafety@mtaloy.edu EEO is the LAW Mount Aloysius College is an equal opportunity employer, and does not tolerate unlawful discrimination against any person on the basis of age, ancestry, color, disability or handicap, national origin, race, religious creed, gender, sexual orientation, genetic information or veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact us at 814-886-6500 or by email at HumanResources@mtaloy.edu. Employment will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with College policy. Mount Aloysius College"}, "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d098156f9c01982e34a60801d2&id=8a7887a8a0abfc8001a0ed97475e2576&source=&lang=en": {"title": "Nursing Faculty - Medical-Surgical (FT) - DuBois", "description": "Careers | Mount Aloysius College Home Position: Nursing Faculty - Medical-Surgical (FT) - DuBois Location: DuBois, PA Job Id: 242 # of Openings: 1 Mount Aloysius College, repeatedly recognized by ModernThink as a \u201cGreat College to Work For,\u201d seeks highly qualified nurse educators with medical-surgical nursing experience to join our team of Nursing Faculty in DuBois, PA. Current Opening This open faculty position offers a regular, full-time, 9-month appointment with primary teaching obligations during the core academic year from August \u2013 May.\u00a0 The successful candidate is responsible for a workload of 24 credit hours or equivalent per academic year; will teach undergraduate theory and clinical courses, typically in fundamentals, adult health, behavioral health, geriatric, and medical/surgical topics; and develop curricula while also assessing learning outcomes. The College Administration plans for a robust, in-person experience for students.\u00a0 To support this goal, faculty are expected to have a regular presence on the DuBois campus (5 days per week required) to engage with students both inside and outside of the classroom and to participate in meetings/committee work, advising, office hours, college events and other activities. Mount Aloysius College offers a generous benefits package for full-time employees including but not limited to: medical/health, dental, vision, and life insurance; short-term and long-term disability insurance; Retirement plan match; tuition remission; and an employee assistance program, among others. Qualifications Master's degree in Nursing (MSN) required.\u00a0 Doctorate preferred (PhD, DNP, EdD) earned or in final semester/ABD with pending graduation date.\u00a0 Prior classroom and clinical teaching experience at the collegiate level strongly preferred. Valid, unencumbered license as a registered nurse or advanced practice nurse in Pennsylvania required. Minimum 3-4 years of nursing experience, with at least two years in behavioral health nursing and a demonstrated ability to perform at a high level is required. This role is not budgeted for visa sponsorship at this time; all candidates must be authorized to\u00a0work in the US at the time of submission of their application. About Mount Aloysius College\u2019s Expansion into DuBois, PA Mount Aloysius College is bringing nursing education to DuBois beginning Fall 2026!\u00a0 Students can complete pre-nursing coursework this fall, and begin their path toward a rewarding healthcare career close to home with a two year associates degree. Through a new collaboration with Penn Highlands Healthcare, eligible nursing students may receive up to $48,000 in combined financial support, along with hands-on clinical opportunities and pathways to employment after graduation. Commitment to Diversity Mount Aloysius is committed to building an inclusive community that values each person and respects diversity of all kinds \u2013 diversity of thought, experience, culture, ethnicity, religion, gender/gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, etc. to create a workplace where everyone participates and is able to contribute their own unique gifts, talents and perspectives. Application Instructions Apply online at http://www.mtaloy.edu/employment-opportunities.\u00a0 All applicants should submit a resume with an accompanying cover letter.\u00a0 Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled.\u00a0 Applicants needing reasonable accommodation to participate in the application process should contact the Office of Human Resources at (814) 886-6519. Mount Aloysius College is an Equal Opportunity Employer Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by REQUIRED NOTICES The Mount Aloysius College Annual Security and Fire Safety Report contains statistics for the three previous calendar years of reported crimes that occurred on our campuses, in certain off-campus buildings or properties owned or controlled by Mount Aloysius College, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from our campuses. This annual report is required by federal law, and contains information regarding campus security and personal safety, including institutional policies, crime prevention, crime reporting policies, and fire safety. The report also includes our current Sexual Assault and Misconduct Policies. The 2024 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online. You may also request a printed copy from Mount Aloysius College's Office of Campus Safety, located in Ihmsen Hall 112, by calling (814) 886-6327 or via email to CampusSafety@mtaloy.edu EEO is the LAW Mount Aloysius College is an equal opportunity employer, and does not tolerate unlawful discrimination against any person on the basis of age, ancestry, color, disability or handicap, national origin, race, religious creed, gender, sexual orientation, genetic information or veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact us at 814-886-6500 or by email at HumanResources@mtaloy.edu. Employment will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with College policy. Mount Aloysius College"}}, "rows": {"https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d098156f9c01982e34a60801d2&id=8a78839e9f443598019f4dbb219619b9&source=&lang=en": {"school_id": 1143, "posting_url": "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d098156f9c01982e34a60801d2&id=8a78839e9f443598019f4dbb219619b9&source=&lang=en", "job_title_in_post": "ASN Chairperson - Cresson", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d098156f9c01982e34a60801d2&id=8a78839ea06420ea01a068ae6d3432f9&sou